<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-FOCUS-Australian union bans Indonesian ships.</title>
<headline>RTRS-FOCUS-Australian union bans Indonesian ships.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's powerful Maritime Union on Wednesday launched rolling bans on Indonesian shipping to protest against the arrest of Indonesian labour leaders and Canberra's &quot;failure&quot; to press Jakarta on human rights.</p>
<p>The lightning bans, called at short notice and designed to hold up ships for 24 hours, could apply on an irregular basis to all types of commodity exports to Indonesia, the union said.</p>
<p>Australia's nearest Asian neighbour bought A$2.4 billion (US$1.9 billion) worth of Australian commodities in 1995, covering grains, minerals, livestock and refined petroleum.</p>
</text>
